SUMMARY:Local Art Live!
DESCRIPTION:Thursday June 18th\, 2026\nDoors | 6:00 PM\nShow | 7:00 PM \nEvent Ticket | $19.30 + Fees \nThis event is all ages – 21+ With Valid ID Required to Drink\nCome hungry! Snacks and light bites will be available at the canteen.\n—————————————————\nPresented by Mickey’s Black Box\n—————————————————\nCome out and enjoy a great night of live music\, artistic expression\, and delicious drinks – highlighting the incredible talent in our backyard! \nFeaturing Artists – Hot Dad Calendar\, Muddy Ruckus (on tour from Maine)\, thequietcampaign\, & Caulfield’s Radio \nHot Dad Calendar\nComing in hot out of Pennsylvania\, Hot Dad Calendar is the authentic result of three friends combining their own distinctive styles and personalities to bring a fresh\, nostalgic sound to the alternative/indie rock scene. Their first full-length studio album\, “The Fear We Find in Safe Spaces\,” recorded at Miner Street Recordings in Philadelphia\, PA is available now!  \nMuddy Ruckus (on tour from Maine)\nMuddy Ruckus is a wild-hearted\, feral psyche rock duo known for transforming minimalist instrumentation into a full-throttle sonic eruption. Fronted by guitarist/songwriter Ryan Flaherty and drummer/vocalist Erika Stahl\, the band delivers a sound far bigger than two people should be able to conjure. Stahl thunders on a custom suitcase kick drum while Flaherty runs his guitar through a maze of two guitar amps and one bass amp simultaneously-an alchemy that turns raw voltage into atmosphere\, grit\, and cinematic fire. \nthequietcampaign \nCaulfield’s Radio\nRaw elements of punk and classic rock merge with intelligent songwriting in the formation of Caulfield’s Radio. The four-man group derives its name from JD Salinger’s Catcher In The Rye\, and creates a dynamic and tension-filled sound that reflects the angst and rebellion found in the classic novel. Influenced equally by the likes of John Prine and Robert Johnson\, you can expect a spectrum of funk\, hard rock and Cuban rhythms with a combination of cover songs and original material. \nFeaturing Local Vendors – Manic Motif\, Artsy Shroom\, Lititz Music Co.\, Nona Holland Print\, Sarah Keane\, & Lynn Shirk\n—————————————————\n*Ticket Alert*  \nTickets for Mickey’s Black Box are sold through TicketMaster\, via our website\, or in person at our Box Office. Any tickets purchased elsewhere will not be honored and we are not responsible for tickets purchased from any 3rd party sellers.  Do not google the name of the band to search for tickets.  Go to Mickeysblackbox.com ONLY. Mickeysblackbox.com will never direct you anywhere but the official TicketMaster event site. \n\nAll bags are subject are to search upon entry. Tickets are non-refundable\, save for instances in which performances are cancelled by Mickey’s Black Box. For more information about our venue or to make an ADA request\, please visit the FAQ page of our website: https://mickeysblackbox.com/faq/ or call our box office line at (717) 723 – 8463.
URL:https://mickeysblackbox.com/event/local-art-live-2/
LOCATION:Mickey’s Black Box\, 101 Rock Lititz Boulevard\, Lititz\, PA\, 17543\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://mickeysblackbox.com/app/uploads/2026/03/LocalArtLiveJune18final-e1773266454898.png
